ence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Hillary Scholten (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Hillary Scholten seeks a third term in a west Michigan district that leans Democratic by about four points but has a Republican heritage. She enters the general election with a decisive financial advantage, roughly $3 million raised and $1.5 million on hand, while Republican Terri DeBoer, a first-time candidate who won an outsider-flavored primary, has raised under $1 million and holds only about $70,000. No outside groups are currently spending against the incumbent.\n\nWith no general-election polling available, the picture rests on fundamentals, and they favor Scholten across the board. All ten expert ratings place the race in the Safe or Solid Democratic column, and prediction markets price her win probability near 96%. DeBoer's path depends on a favorable national environment and strong conservative turnout, but the evidence points to a comfortable incumbent win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9846, "margin": 15.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9771, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9798, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9738, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.976, "margin": 15.2}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9772, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9828, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.972, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9845, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9812, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9777, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9742, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9773, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9787, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-